IMPORT prelude

-- Housing Developers (Control and Licensing) Act 1965 (Singapore) -- what counts as housing development and needs a licence (ss 2,
-- 4), the misuse of the words "housing developer" (s 6), suspension and appeals (ss 4(10), 7, 12(3)), the Project Account that holds
-- buyers' money and its protection on the developer's insolvency (s 9), audited accounts open to the public (s 10), the secrecy of
-- buyers' particulars (s 11(4)), who may not run a licensed developer (s 25), and the penalties and composition sums (ss 4, 6, 9, 10,
-- 11, 12A, 17A, 23, 25, 26, 27A).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021), informal
-- consolidation "version in force from 1/7/2025", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/HDCLA1965.txt. The latest amendment
-- annotated in the text is Act 15 of 2025 (wef 01/07/2025).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: anyone in Singapore who buys a new private home from a developer is a
-- "purchaser" under this Act, and the licence, the Project Account and the published accounts are what protect that purchaser's
-- money. (An automated count found 4 of the 527 deposited Singapore Acts citing it by this title; that undercounts and is not a
-- measure of importance.) SCOPED to the provisions a home buyer meets. NOT ENCODED: the application paperwork (s 4(2)-(4)); the
-- licence bars in s 5 (capital, deposits, fraud and money-laundering disqualifications); alteration notices (s 8); the
-- anti-money-laundering programme duties of Part 3A beyond the s 12A penalty; auditors (s 13, 13A); investigation powers and the
-- Minister's rescue powers (ss 14-21); the rule-making list (s 22) -- the deposit limits, progressive payment schedule, standard
-- form contract and show-unit rules are left to rules under s 22 (not named in the deposit), which were NOT retrieved; immunity (s 24); officer
-- liability (s 27); exemptions (s 28); and the Public Prosecutor's consent (s 29).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Housing Developers (Control and Licensing) Act 1965 -- developers and buyers`

§§ `2 and 4(1), (8) -- housing development needs a licence`

-- s 2: "housing development" means "the business of -- (a) developing; (b) providing the money for developing or for the purchase of,
-- MORE THAN 4 UNITS of housing accommodation; or (c) developing and providing the money for the purchase of more than 4 units".
-- "housing developer" excludes a licensed bank or a licensed insurer "so long as such bank or insurer only lends or provides money
-- for housing development".
-- s 4(1): "No housing development may be carried out or undertaken in Singapore except by a housing developer who or which is in
-- possession of a written licence from the Controller". (8): fine up to $100,000 "and shall also be liable to imprisonment for a term
-- not exceeding 5 years".
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `building homes for sale`
    `financing the building or purchase of homes`
    `building homes and financing their purchase`
    `a licensed bank only lending for the development`
    `a licensed insurer only lending for the development`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity, `units` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is housing development by a housing developer` IF
        `units` GREATER THAN 4
    AND CONSIDER `the activity`
        WHEN `a licensed bank only lending for the development` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a licensed insurer only lending for the development` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity, `units` IS A NUMBER, `holds a written licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `carrying it out is an offence under section 4(8)` IF
        `the activity is housing development by a housing developer` `the activity` `units`
    AND (NOT `holds a written licence`)

§§ `4(10), 7 and 12(3) -- suspension and appeals to the Minister`

-- s 7(1): on any listed ground "the Controller may revoke, or suspend for a period NOT EXCEEDING 12 MONTHS, any licence"; (2) only after
-- notifying the intention and giving "an opportunity to submit reasons or an explanation".
-- s 4(10): appeal against grant, refusal or conditions "within 10 days after it is notified ... to the Minister whose decision is final".
-- s 7(3): against revocation or suspension "within 30 days", the Minister's decision "is final and shall not be questioned in any
-- court". s 12(3): against a decision on a sale or reconstruction of the business "within 14 days", in the same words as s 7(3).
GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER, `notified and heard first` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension is within section 7` IF
        `months` AT MOST 12
    AND `notified and heard first`

DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `a licence refusal or condition`
    `a revocation or suspension`
    `a decision on selling the business`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days to appeal to the Minister` IS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a licence refusal or condition` THEN 10
    WHEN `a revocation or suspension` THEN 30
    WHEN `a decision on selling the business` THEN 14

-- Literal reading only: s 4(10) says "final" but, unlike ss 7(3) and 12(3), does not add "shall not be questioned in any court".
-- What that difference does in court is not decided here.
GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act expressly says the Minister's decision shall not be questioned in court` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a licence refusal or condition` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `9 -- the Project Account`

-- s 9(1): every licensed developer "must open and keep an account (called ... a Project Account) with a bank or finance company for
-- each building project"; (3) buyers' purchase moneys required by the rules must be paid in; (4) no withdrawals "except as authorised
-- by rules". (10): s 9 does not apply where "all the units ... will not be offered for sale ... before the completion of the building
-- project", or where the developer furnishes security of "not less than 140% of the total cost of construction" as certified by the
-- architect.
GIVEN `no unit is offered for sale before completion` IS A BOOLEAN, `security as a percentage of construction cost` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Project Account is required` IF
        (NOT `no unit is offered for sale before completion`)
    AND `security as a percentage of construction cost` LESS THAN 140

-- s 9(5): moneys in the Project Account are "deemed not to form part of the property of the licensed housing developer" if (a) it
-- compounds or arranges with creditors or has a receiving or adjudication order made against it, or (b) being a company, goes into
-- voluntary or compulsory liquidation. (6): they vest in the official receiver, trustee or liquidator, to be applied for the
-- authorised purposes; only the balance after the sale and purchase obligations are discharged goes to the general creditors.
DECLARE Event IS ONE OF
    `no insolvency event`
    `a composition with creditors`
    `a receiving or adjudication order`
    `a voluntary liquidation`
    `a compulsory liquidation`

GIVEN `the event` IS AN Event
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Project Account money is ring-fenced from the developer's property` IF
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `no insolvency event` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `10 -- audited accounts open to the public`

-- s 10(1): within 6 months "(or any extended period that the Controller may grant under subsection (2)) after the close of every
-- financial year", forward to the Controller AND make available "for a continuous period of at least 24 months" at its office or on
-- its website "for inspection by the public without charge" its audited accounts and auditor's report. (2): the Controller may extend
-- "but not more than once and such extension must not in any case exceed 6 months". (3): fine up to $50,000.
GIVEN `number of extensions` IS A NUMBER, `extension months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the extension is within section 10(2)` IF
        `number of extensions` AT MOST 1
    AND `extension months` AT MOST 6

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the smaller of` IS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- An extension above 6 months cannot be granted, so at most 6 months of it are counted.
GIVEN `months after year end` IS A NUMBER, `extension granted` IS A NUMBER, `months open for inspection` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the developer complied with section 10(1)` IF
        `months after year end` AT MOST (6 + `the smaller of` `extension granted` 6)
    AND `months open for inspection` AT LEAST 24

§§ `11(4) -- buyers' particulars are secret`

-- s 11(4): no one may disclose particulars of "any purchaser, intending purchaser or assignee" received under s 11 unless (a) for the
-- purposes of s 11 "with the Minister's prior approval"; (b) "in the form of statistics which do not identify" them; (c) to the
-- Chief Statistician on a direction under the Statistics Act; (d) already in the public domain; or (e) for proceedings for an offence
-- under the Act or a report of them. (5): $10,000 or 12 months or both.
DECLARE Disclosure IS ONE OF
    `for section 11 purposes with the Minister's prior approval`
    `as statistics that identify no buyer`
    `to the Chief Statistician on direction`
    `of particulars already public`
    `for an offence prosecution under the Act`
    `to a property marketing firm`
    `to a journalist`

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is permitted` IF
    CONSIDER `the disclosure`
    WHEN `to a property marketing firm` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `to a journalist` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `25 -- who may not hold a responsible position`

-- s 25(1)(a): a person "convicted of an offence (whether in Singapore or elsewhere) involving fraud or dishonesty" must not hold a
-- responsible position "until the expiry of 5 years after the LATER of" the conviction date and, if imprisoned, the release date;
-- (b) an undischarged bankrupt must not; (ba) a person convicted of a money laundering, proliferation financing or terrorism financing
-- offence must not (no time limit); (c) a holder "must cease to hold that position if he or she suspends payment to or compounds with
-- his or her creditors". (2): a holder in a licensed developer that is wound up by the court (or dissolved) must not, "except with the
-- Minister's written approval", hold a responsible position "in any other licensed housing developer".
-- Penalties (3), (4): $50,000 or 3 years or both; for (1)(ba), $100,000.
DECLARE Person HAS
    `convicted of fraud or dishonesty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years since conviction` IS A NUMBER
    `years since release from prison` IS A NUMBER
    `an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `convicted of a money laundering offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has compounded with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `held a responsible position in a developer wound up by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has the Minister's written approval` IS A BOOLEAN

-- With no imprisonment, the fixtures set the release figure equal to the conviction figure.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may hold a responsible position` IF
        (    (NOT `the person`'s `convicted of fraud or dishonesty`)
         OR  `the smaller of` (`the person`'s `years since conviction`) (`the person`'s `years since release from prison`) AT LEAST 5)
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `an undischarged bankrupt`)
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `convicted of a money laundering offence`)
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `has compounded with creditors`)
    AND (    (NOT `the person`'s `held a responsible position in a developer wound up by the court`)
         OR  `the person`'s `has the Minister's written approval`)

§§ `4(8), (9), 6(2), 9(11), 10(3), 11(5), 12A(2), 17A(4), (5), 23(2), 25(3), 26 -- maximum penalties`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `developing without a licence`
    `breaching a licence condition`
    `calling itself a housing developer without a licence`
    `breaching the Project Account rules`
    `failing to publish audited accounts`
    `disclosing buyers' particulars`
    `taking money from an anonymous source`
    `obstructing a show-unit inspection`
    `ignoring a show-unit direction`
    `ignoring a Controller's direction`
    `a disqualified person holding a responsible position`
    `an offence with no penalty provided`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `developing without a licence` THEN 100000
    WHEN `breaching a licence condition` THEN 100000
    WHEN `calling itself a housing developer without a licence` THEN 100000
    WHEN `breaching the Project Account rules` THEN 50000
    WHEN `failing to publish audited accounts` THEN 50000
    WHEN `disclosing buyers' particulars` THEN 10000
    WHEN `taking money from an anonymous source` THEN 100000
    WHEN `obstructing a show-unit inspection` THEN 10000
    WHEN `ignoring a show-unit direction` THEN 10000
    WHEN `ignoring a Controller's direction` THEN 50000
    WHEN `a disqualified person holding a responsible position` THEN 50000
    WHEN `an offence with no penalty provided` THEN 50000

-- 0 where the section provides a fine only.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `developing without a licence` THEN 60
    WHEN `breaching a licence condition` THEN 36
    WHEN `calling itself a housing developer without a licence` THEN 36
    WHEN `breaching the Project Account rules` THEN 12
    WHEN `disclosing buyers' particulars` THEN 12
    WHEN `obstructing a show-unit inspection` THEN 6
    WHEN `a disqualified person holding a responsible position` THEN 36
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 23(2): a further fine "not exceeding $5,000 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction".
GIVEN `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine for ignoring a direction including daily fines` IS
    50000 + 5000 * `days continued after conviction`

-- s 27A(1): the Controller may compound a prescribed compoundable offence "by collecting ... a sum not exceeding one half of the amount
-- of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence". Which offences are prescribed is in rules NOT retrieved.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum composition sum` IS
    `the maximum fine` `the offence` / 2
